\paragraph{Physical-model adequacy.} Condition~(ii) concerns the detector model. It is the simulation's per event, varied only by the drawn detector bands (\Sef{sec:joint5d-calibration}, each at $\pm1\sigma$) and by the linear surrogate for the five lateral bands. The surrogate has been checked only for the symmetry of its endpoints. The analysis's systematic set (App.~ef{app:statmethods}) has no recoil-energy-scale band, so the completeness of the hadronic response is not established (\Sef{sec:joint5d-response}). Condition~(iii) concerns the interaction-model prior, the analysis's set of \jtModelBands{} interaction-model reweighting bands, with every band drawn in every pseudo-experiment. Negative weights in two of them, LowQ2\_1 and HighQ2\_1, are clipped per universe. Measured on the pilot, the effect of clipping them rather than keeping them is at most 0.35\% of a band's shift in whitened norm. Condition~(v) concerns the neutrino-energy range. The GiBUU sample contains no events with $E_{
u}>\SI{20}{GeV}$ (\Sef{sec:eavailw-band}), and its truth outside the test domain ($\pPar\ge\SI{6}{GeV/c}$, with truncated $E_{
u}$) enters through the migrations into the domain cells. No prediction contains events with $E_{
u}>\SI{100}{GeV}$; only the data's flux integral stops there, and the omission is negligible. The use of the Tune~v1 composition below the fine grid in (i) is also a modeling choice of this kind.
